  L('m2c8-2', 'm2c8', 'Evaluating continuous-outcome and classification models',
`**Continuous outcomes**
• **MSE** = average squared error; **RMSE** = √MSE (same units as y, penalises big errors).
• **MAE** = average absolute error (robust to outliers).
• **R²** = 1 − SSE/SST.

**Classification – confusion matrix**: TP, FP, TN, FN.
• **Accuracy** = (TP + TN) / total — misleading with imbalanced data.
• **Precision** = TP / (TP + FP): of the flagged cases, how many are real?
• **Recall / sensitivity / TPR** = TP / (TP + FN): of the real cases, how many did we catch?
• **Specificity / TNR** = TN / (TN + FP); **FPR** = 1 − specificity.
• **F1** = 2·P·R / (P + R): harmonic mean of precision and recall.

Example: TP 40, FP 10, FN 20, TN 930 → accuracy 97%, precision 0.80, recall 0.667, F1 ≈ 0.727.`,
