  L('m2c9-5', 'm2c9', 'TF-IDF weighting',
`**TF-IDF** weights a word by how important it is to **this document** relative to the **whole collection**:

• **TF** (term frequency) = count of term in the document / number of terms in the document.
• **IDF** (inverse document frequency) = log(N / dfₜ), where N = number of documents and dfₜ = number of documents containing the term.
• **TF-IDF = TF × IDF**.

Words that appear everywhere ("the", "company") get IDF ≈ 0; words frequent in one document but rare overall get high weight → they characterise that document.

Example (log base 10): a term appears 5 times in a 100-word document → TF = 0.05. It appears in 10 of 1,000 documents → IDF = log(100) = 2. TF-IDF = 0.10.`,
['TF = count / doc length', 'IDF = log(N / df)', 'TF-IDF = TF × IDF', 'Common words → near zero; distinctive words → high']);
