  L('m2c10-1', 'm2c10', 'Generative AI taxonomy: modalities and algorithms',
`**Generative AI** creates new content resembling its training data.

By **content modality**: text (LLMs), images, audio/speech, video, code, synthetic tabular data, and **multimodal** models combining several.

By **modelling algorithm**:
• **Generative adversarial networks (GANs)**: a **generator** creates samples and a **discriminator** tries to tell real from fake; they train against each other. Sharp images; unstable training, mode collapse. Use: synthetic data, deepfakes.
• **Variational autoencoders (VAEs)**: encoder–decoder with a probabilistic latent space; sample from it to generate. Stable, smoother/blurrier outputs.
• **Diffusion models**: learn to reverse a gradual noising process; state of the art for images (e.g. Stable Diffusion).
• **Autoregressive transformers**: generate one token at a time, each conditioned on the previous ones — the basis of LLMs.
