  L('m2c10-5', 'm2c10', 'RNNs, LSTMs and transformers for word relationships',
`• **RNN**: reads text **sequentially**, carrying a hidden state. Captures order, but suffers from **vanishing gradients** → forgets distant words; cannot be parallelised over the sequence.
• **LSTM**: adds a **cell state** and **gates** (forget, input, output) to keep long-range information. Better memory, still sequential and slower.
• **Transformer** (2017): drops recurrence and uses **self-attention**: every token directly attends to every other token, weighting their relevance. Adds **positional encodings** for order; **multi-head attention** captures different relationships in parallel.
  + Captures long-range dependencies, highly **parallelisable** → trains on huge corpora → basis of LLMs (BERT, GPT).
  − Attention cost grows with the **square of sequence length**, limiting context windows.`,
