  L('m2c10-8', 'm2c10', 'Context length and statelessness',
`• **Context length (context window)**: the maximum number of **tokens** (prompt + conversation + output) the model can process at once. Text beyond it is truncated or must be summarised/chunked. Long contexts cost more compute and latency, and models may pay less attention to information in the **middle** of long inputs ("lost in the middle").
